lides','',0),(199,1,'2013-09-12 08:14:08','2013-09-12 08:14:08','','Check out last minute flight, hotel & vacation offers!','Save up to 40%!','publish','closed','closed','','check-out-last-minute-flight-hotel-vacation-offers','','','2014-05-18 16:24:48','2014-05-18 16:24:48','',0,'http://www.kajag.com/themes/book_your_travel_wordpress/?post_type=sequence-slides&#038;p=199',0,'sequence-slides','',0),(503,1,'2013-11-28 20:05:25','2013-11-28 20:05:25','The reality of the journey from Belgrade to Prague is grey and rainy… high-rises and graffiti with different currency at every turn (non EU countries) and strange salad combinations.\r\n<h4>Day 1</h4>\r\nFlight from Venice to Prague. Explore Old town, the heart of Prague, with its well preserved13th century houses and churches. Here, you’ll find the Old Town Hall, the Municipal House and the Estates Theatre. The Old Town Square is home to the famous Astronomical Clock which draws onlookers who gather to observe the skeleton ringing the bell and the other figurines which appear. When the bell chimes the hour, a trumpeter sounds a fanfare from the top of the tower. Hop off and see The Metronome monument, which is situated where the Stalin memorial statue once stood, and enjoy stunning views of the city.\r\nWe will spend the night in a four star hotel in the center of Prague.\r\n<h4>Day 2</h4>\r\nWe will drive from Prague to Brno. A tour visit of Brno which includes the most interesting sights: St. Peter and Paul Cathedral, Denis Park, Cabbage Market (Zelný Trh) with baroque fountain Parnas, the Holy Trinity Column, Capuchin Crypt, Old Town Hall, Freedom Square with Plague Pillar, Klein´s Palace, House of Lords of Lipá, St. James church. We will spend the night in a four star hotel in the center of Brno.\r\n<h4>Day 3</h4>\r\nWe will drive from Brno to Bratislava. During our tour in Bratislava we will show you the most important places and historic sights of the city. We will guide you through the Old Town starting from Bratislava’s oldest remaining fortification, the 13th Michalska Gate. The next point will be the Primate Palace, one of the most beautiful buildings in Bratislava. Then we will walk to the gothic St. Martin’s Cathedral, discover the 15th -century Town Hall which is still in use today as well as the Presidential Palace and the Bratislavian Castle towering over the city. Finally we will head to the Slavin Monument, dedicated to the Soviet soldiers who liberated Bratislava in 1945. This cemetery is also a popular vantage point where you will see breathtaking view of the entire Bratislava. We will spend the night in a five star hotel in the center of Bratislava.\r\n<h4>Day 4</h4>\r\nOff to Szeged. The program includes the Castle Museum, Móra Ferenc Museum, the Black House, the Treasury of the Diocese of Csanád, the Dömötör-Tower. A walk in the historcial past and an introduction of the collection of the museums. Night drive on a luxury bus to Novi Sad.\r\n<h4>Day 5</h4>\r\nGet yourself familiar with Sremski Karlovci (visit the Cathedral Church and the Chapel of Peace)· Taste quality Fruska Gora wines in one of the wineries in Karlovac· Visit at least three monasteries in Fruska Gora· Rest of the tour is arranged between the tour guide and the group (visit to one more of the monasteries, some of Fruska Gora lakes, wineries, …). Drive to Belgrade where will we spend the night.\r\n<h4>Day 6</h4>\r\nFunny and interesting sightseeing: The Republic Square, Bohemian Quarter (Skadarlija), the oldest part of Belgrade with Ottoman heritage, „Sillicon valley“, Zoo, Kalemegdan park, Belgrade fortress, The „Victor“ the most famous symbol of Belgrade, the confluence of the Sava and the Danube rivers. Saborna church, cafe „?“, Knez Mihailova street. Remains of the afternoon and evening free to do your own thing.\r\n<h4>Day 7</h4>\r\nOur tour ends after breakfast and included onward departure transfer to the airport.\r\n<h4>Price includes</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Transportation between the program</li>\r\n	<li>Meals</li>\r\n	<li>Services of the guide of the program</li>\r\n	<li>Museum tickets</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>Price do not include</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Other costs not offered in this program</li>\r\n	<li>Tip for your tour guide</li>\r\n</ul>','Nha trang','Get yourself familiar with Sremski Karlovci (visit the Cathedral Church and the Chapel of Peace)· Taste quality Fruska Gora wines in one of the wineries in Karlovac· Visit at least three monasteries in Fruska Gora· Rest of the tour is arranged between the tour guide and the group (visit to one more of the monasteries, some of Fruska Gora lakes, wineries, …). Drive to Belgrade where will we spend the night.','publish','closed','closed','','prague-to-belgrade','','','2014-06-01 04:12:52','2014-06-01 04:12:52','',0,'http://www.kajag.com/themes/book_your_travel_wordpress/?post_type=tour&#038;p=503',0,'tour','',0),(649,1,'2014-06-04 04:41:49','2014-06-04 04:41:49','Business Travel','Business Travel','','publish','open','open','','business-travel','','','2014-06-04 04:41:49','2014-06-04 04:41:49','',0,'http://localhost/wp-cms/vietaustravel.au/?page_id=649',0,'page','',0),(648,1,'2014-06-04 04:41:20','2014-06-04 04:41:20','Interpreter  Services','Interpreter  Services','','inherit','open','open','','646-revision-v1','','','2014-06-04 04:41:20','2014-06-04 04:41:20','',646,'http://localhost/wp-cms/vietaustravel.au/646-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(647,1,'2014-06-04 04:41:20','2014-06-04 04:41:20',' ','','','publish','open','open','','647','','','2014-06-04 04:41:20','2014-06-04 04:41:20','',0,'http://localhost/wp-cms/vietaustravel.au/647/',8,'nav_menu_item','',0),(644,1,'2014-06-04 04:37:23','2014-06-04 04:37:23','Vietnam Visa Services','Vietnam Visa Services ','','inherit','open','open','','642-revision-v1','','','2014-06-04 04:37:23','2014-06-04 04:37:23','',642,'http://localhost/wp-cms/vietaustravel.au/642-revision-v1/',0,'revision','',0),(516,1,'2014-05-18 16:20:38','2014-05-18 16:20:38',' ','','','pu